`crimes context` confirms one medium and two low findings, with no likely tests or related design-system files detected. I’d refactor `Card` into a non-interactive layout container with an explicit semantic action.

```tsx
import styles from "./Card.module.css";

type CardProps = {
  children: React.ReactNode;
  onActivate: () => void;
};

export function Card({ children, onActivate }: CardProps) {
  return (
    <article className={styles.card}>
      <div className={styles.content}>{children}</div>

      <aside className={styles.sidebar}>sidebar</aside>

      <button
        type="button"
        className={styles.action}
        onClick={onActivate}
      >
        Open card
      </button>
    </article>
  );
}
```

The associated CSS should:

```css
.card {
  container: card / inline-size;
  display: grid;
  grid-template-columns:
    minmax(0, 1fr)
    minmax(var(--card-sidebar-min), var(--card-sidebar-max));
  inline-size: 100%;
  max-inline-size: var(--card-max-inline-size);
  padding: var(--space-card);
  color: var(--color-text-primary);
  background: var(--color-surface-accent);
  border: var(--border-width-subtle) solid var(--color-border-subtle);
  box-shadow: var(--shadow-card);
}

.content {
  min-inline-size: 0;
  font-size: clamp(
    var(--font-size-body-min),
    var(--font-size-body-fluid),
    var(--font-size-body-max)
  );
}

.sidebar {
  color: var(--color-text-secondary);
}

.action {
  color: var(--color-action);
  outline-color: var(--color-focus-ring);
}

@container card (inline-size < 40rem) {
  .card {
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
  }
}
```

How this maps to the findings:

- `accessible_interaction_risk`: remove `onClick` from the outer `<div>` and expose the action as a native `<button>`. It automatically supplies keyboard activation, focusability, and button semantics. Because `children` is unrestricted `ReactNode`, wrapping the entire card in a button could create invalid nested interactions; a dedicated action is safer. If the action navigates, use `<a href>` instead.
- `design_token_escape`: move presentation out of JSX and replace the nine raw colors, spacing, shadow, and sizing literals with established theme tokens. The proposed token names are illustrative; their values should live in the shared theme, not be redefined locally as aliases for the same literals.
- `responsive_fragility`: remove the fixed `800px`, `720px`, `600px`, and sidebar widths. Use `inline-size: 100%`, a tokenized maximum, `minmax(0, 1fr)`, fluid `clamp()` typography, and a container-query collapse based on the card’s available space.

Since context found no likely tests, I’d add a component test verifying that the button is reachable by keyboard and activates with Enter/Space, plus a narrow-container layout test ensuring the card does not overflow. No files were changed.
